    "questionText": "Jamie: – As far as I see, you are quite good at communicating with your plants in the garden. You never return with an empty basket and your vase is always shining with new flowers. Sandra: – Yeah, you have a point. And more importantly, it's not random. I always know the correct time to gather a new bunch of flowers from certain plants. Jamie: – ---- Sandra: – Strikingly, the order of species leafing out any one garden is almost identical from year to year, with some species always starting the process early and others always late. Jamie: – So, it means that a gardener just needs to observe her plants to learn their usual flowering times.",
