    "questionText": "Christine: - Have you ever wondered why we rub our eyes when we feel tired? Lee: - ---- Christine: - It sounds like a rational reason, but scientists have a different view on why we rub our eyes because of tiredness. They say it triggers the oculocardiac reflex, which lowers the heart rate and helps us relax when we're tired. Lee: - That's really interesting. I've never thought the eyes may have an impact on the heart and produce a calming effect.",
