    "passage": "At a time when sharks were feared and killed indiscriminately, Eugenie Clark re-envisioned marine biology. In her book, Lady with a Spear, the American ichthyologist suggested that the best way to study sharks was to observe them in their natural habitat through direct underwater diving, (22)---- relying solely on specimens caught by fishing boats, and therefore helped form the basis of modern field-based marine research. Eugenie's advocacy began while conducting research expeditions in the Red Sea, where she led diving tours to persuade the public against viewing sharks purely as dangerous predators in order to (23)---- the widespread killing of sharks for sport. And in 1955, at a time when few women held leadership positions in marine science, she founded the Cape Haze Marine Laboratory, which enforced a set of research protocols (24)---- the careless capture of endangered marine species for public display. Over the course of her life, Eugenie achieved many firsts, notably becoming the first female scientist (25)---- the International Game Fish Association's scientific advisory board in 1975. (26)----, she paved the way for women marine biologists and made a male-dominated field accessible to everyone.",
    "questionText": "Parçadaki (22) numaralı boşluğa aşağıdakilerden hangisi getirilmelidir?",
