    "questionText": "Despite growing awareness of coral reef fragility within the diving community, the responsible management of divers remains critically important. Although mindful of how delicate the underwater environment is, a recreational diver still retains natural curiosity and the desire to make a brief, guided dive as memorable as possible. ---- Clearly, the potential damage caused by such curiosity must be minimised wherever possible, but the relative invisibility of these small, cumulative acts to all but the divers themselves makes the issue difficult to monitor.",
