    "questionText": "A processing disorder is characterised by a difficulty in interpreting sensory input, leading to poor coordination between perception and physical response. Therefore, people with a processing disorder can have difficulties with balance and with fine motor tasks. ---- Generally, individuals who are identified as having a processing disorder before the age of seven and who receive intensive occupational therapy can make significant progress. There is, however, a great deal of variation among individuals in temperament, access to therapy, and the will to overcome a processing disorder. All these factors combine to determine the ultimate outcome of this condition.",
