    "passage": "Mumps is a contagious viral illness that mostly affects children but can occur in adults as well. It is caused by the mumps virus, which is spread (17)---- respiratory droplets or by direct contact with saliva from an infected person. Once someone (18)---- with the virus, an incubation period of about 16-18 days passes before symptoms appear. It produces painful swelling of the salivary glands that typically lasts about a week and is sometimes (19)---- by a mild fever and fatigue. (20)---- the symptoms of mumps are usually mild and resolve without complications, treatment can almost always be carried out at home with rest and fluids. Routine care consists of applying warm or cold compresses and taking medications to reduce fever, and (21)---- adequate hydration and soft foods, discomfort while swallowing can be considerably eased.",
    "questionText": "(20). numaralı boşluğa uygun seçeneği işaretleyiniz.",
