    "questionText": "What sparks a subculture? How does one emerge and what are its defining features? In the early 1970s, a new music movement suddenly broke onto the scene in urban Jamaica: dub, or the reggae offshoot. ---- It was a local movement rooted in Jamaican sound-system culture, but its development as part of the global music industry helped to give it recognition and commercial reach. It exalted notions of studio experimentation, yet it also aimed for accessible popular appeal. What was most unusual about dub was that it was a movement led by studio engineers who had begun their careers as sound technicians. They mixed and remixed tracks because it furthered their technical goals, while at the same time they produced original rhythms and promoted each other's studio work.",
