    "questionText": "The Colosseum of Rome is among the world's most famous architectural monuments. In ancient times, visitors from across the empire included the Colosseum among the greatest constructions of the world. The Romans themselves took pride in the structure, repairing and reinforcing it as late as 500 years after it was originally built. However, in spite of the tremendous awe and curiosity that the Colosseum inspires, it is a limited source for the writing of everyday Roman social history. The building attests that the Flavian dynasty (69-96 CE) must have been a period of strong central authority, engineering ambition, and organisational skill. ---- In the Flavian period, the Romans had not yet started inscribing detailed dedicatory texts throughout the structure, a practice of later emperors 100-200 years afterward, that provides historical detail in the later period.",
