    "questionText": "Machine learning (ML) refers to computer software that improves its performance through experience rather than explicit programming. In fact, the term 'learning' is difficult to define and has been the subject of heated debate by computer scientists, statisticians, and cognitive scientists for ages. ---- Learning includes the capacity to adjust internal parameters, maintain a large storehouse of training data, apply statistical inference, discern patterns between variables, generalise to new situations, and perform increasingly complex tasks. Thus, ML systems are computer programs that exhibit one or more of these abilities.",
