    "passage": "",
    "questionText": "Ekip içindeki iletişimin açık ve düzenli olması, yalnızca verimliliği artırmakla kalmaz, aynı zamanda üyeler arasındaki güveni de pekiştirir.",
    "options": {
      "A": "Open and regular communication within a team not only increases efficiency but also reinforces trust among its members.",
      "B": "Communication within a team has no relation to either efficiency or trust.",
      "C": "Teams that avoid communication tend to perform better in terms of efficiency.",
      "D": "Trust among team members is reinforced only when communication is kept to a minimum.",
      "E": "Efficiency within a team depends solely on the number of members rather than communication."
    },
    "correctAnswer": "A",
    "solutionMethod": "✅ Doğru cevap: A) Open and regular communication within a team not only increases efficiency but also reinforces trust among its members.\n\n🔎 Neden doğru? Cümledeki 'yalnızca... kalmaz, aynı zamanda' (not only... but also) yapısı ile 'verimliliği artırmak' (increases efficiency) ve 'güveni pekiştirmek' (reinforces trust) unsurları yalnızca A seçeneğinde eksiksiz şekilde aktarılmıştır.\n\n❌ Diğer seçenekler neden yanlış?\n\nB) İletişimin verimlilik ve güvenle ilgisi olmadığı bilgisi metinle doğrudan çelişir\n\nC) İletişimden kaçınan ekiplerin daha iyi performans gösterdiği bilgisi metinle çelişir\n\nD) Güvenin minimum iletişimle pekiştiği bilgisi metinle doğrudan çelişir\n\nE) Verimliliğin yalnızca üye sayısına bağlı olduğu bilgisi metinde yoktur\n\n🧠 YDS taktiği: Türkçeden İngilizceye çeviri sorularında, 'not only... but also...' gibi korelatif yapıların doğru aktarılması önemlidir.\n\n📌 Öğrenilmesi gereken kelime/kalıp: reinforce (v.): pekiştirmek, güçlendirmek\n\n43-46: Okuma Parçası Sorusu\n\nOkuma Parçası Sorusu (Doğru Bilgi)\n\nRenewable energy microgrids are increasingly being installed in remote island communities that have historically depended on costly diesel generators for electricity. These self-contained systems combine solar panels, small wind turbines, and battery storage to supply power without needing to be connected to a mainland grid. However, experts have long disagreed about how reliably these microgrids can meet demand during periods of poor weather. \"Many assumptions have been made based on overly optimistic modelling of sunlight and wind availability, which has led to some very inflated expectations,\" says energy engineer Priya Nandan of the University of Auckland. \"We felt it was important to test these systems under real-world conditions.\" Nandan is part of a team of researchers who monitored the performance of a microgrid on a small Pacific island for eighteen months to accurately gauge how often backup diesel generators still had to be switched on. By analysing hourly power output records, the researchers found that the system met full demand without any diesel backup on only about 60 to 70 percent of days, a proportion lower than earlier industry estimates. The amount of renewable power actually available was reduced by cloud cover and calm periods, which considerably lowered output during certain seasons. \"Our work has shown that, even shortly after installation, actual performance is often well below the theoretical capacity advertised by manufacturers,\" says Nandan. \"Island microgrids can supply a great deal of clean power, but not nearly as much as has often been claimed.\"",
    "explanation": "✅ Doğru cevap: A) Open and regular communication within a team not only increases efficiency but also reinforces trust among its members.\n\n🔎 Neden doğru? Cümledeki 'yalnızca... kalmaz, aynı zamanda' (not only... but also) yapısı ile 'verimliliği artırmak' (increases efficiency) ve 'güveni pekiştirmek' (reinforces trust) unsurları yalnızca A seçeneğinde eksiksiz şekilde aktarılmıştır.\n\n❌ Diğer seçenekler neden yanlış?\n\nB) İletişimin verimlilik ve güvenle ilgisi olmadığı bilgisi metinle doğrudan çelişir\n\nC) İletişimden kaçınan ekiplerin daha iyi performans gösterdiği bilgisi metinle çelişir\n\nD) Güvenin minimum iletişimle pekiştiği bilgisi metinle doğrudan çelişir\n\nE) Verimliliğin yalnızca üye sayısına bağlı olduğu bilgisi metinde yoktur\n\n🧠 YDS taktiği: Türkçeden İngilizceye çeviri sorularında, 'not only... but also...' gibi korelatif yapıların doğru aktarılması önemlidir.\n\n📌 Öğrenilmesi gereken kelime/kalıp: reinforce (v.): pekiştirmek, güçlendirmek\n\n43-46: Okuma Parçası Sorusu\n\nOkuma Parçası Sorusu (Doğru Bilgi)\n\nRenewable energy microgrids are increasingly being installed in remote island communities that have historically depended on costly diesel generators for electricity. These self-contained systems combine solar panels, small wind turbines, and battery storage to supply power without needing to be connected to a mainland grid. However, experts have long disagreed about how reliably these microgrids can meet demand during periods of poor weather. \"Many assumptions have been made based on overly optimistic modelling of sunlight and wind availability, which has led to some very inflated expectations,\" says energy engineer Priya Nandan of the University of Auckland. \"We felt it was important to test these systems under real-world conditions.\" Nandan is part of a team of researchers who monitored the performance of a microgrid on a small Pacific island for eighteen months to accurately gauge how often backup diesel generators still had to be switched on. By analysing hourly power output records, the researchers found that the system met full demand without any diesel backup on only about 60 to 70 percent of days, a proportion lower than earlier industry estimates. The amount of renewable power actually available was reduced by cloud cover and calm periods, which considerably lowered output during certain seasons. \"Our work has shown that, even shortly after installation, actual performance is often well below the theoretical capacity advertised by manufacturers,\" says Nandan. \"Island microgrids can supply a great deal of clean power, but not nearly as much as has often been claimed.\"",
