    "solutionMethod": "✅ Doğru cevap: D) maintains\n\n🔎 Neden doğru? 'perpetuates a vicious cycle' ifadesi, kısır döngünün sürmesini/devam etmesini sağlamak anlamına gelir; bu nedenle 'maintains' (sürdürür) en yakın anlamlı seçenektir.\n\n❌ Diğer seçenekler neden yanlış?\n\nA) excludes: dışlar\n\nB) terminates: sonlandırır\n\nC) plummets: aniden düşer\n\nE) contradicts: çelişir\n\n🧠 YDS taktiği: Bağlamdan kelime anlamı sorularında, altı çizili kelimenin cümledeki işlevi (olumlu/olumsuz, devam ettirici/sonlandırıcı) belirlenmelidir.\n\n📌 Öğrenilmesi gereken kelime/kalıp: perpetuate (v.): sürdürmek, devam ettirmek\n\nOkuma Parçası Sorusu (Ayrıntı)\n\nDuring the 20th century, numerous engineering breakthroughs in water treatment made it possible to purify or at least significantly improve most of the water sources that have sickened or killed millions of people each year. But the ability to access those treatment systems is concentrated in relatively affluent regions, where the vast majority of water infrastructure investment occurs. The term water security, therefore, encompasses the array of problems faced by the world's most water-stressed inhabitants, who often cannot obtain or do not have access to clean water that could greatly reduce the disease burden under which they suffer. The problems include deficient distribution infrastructure, imbalances between population growth and supply, and the lack of incentive to build treatment facilities in regions with limited economic return. By expanding access to available water interventions, and especially basic sanitation, health officials could prevent millions of deaths annually. Lack of access to clean water and complementary sanitation in turn perpetuates a vicious cycle: poor health impairs productivity and economic development, while low productivity keeps the citizens of the least-developed regions too poor to afford appropriate infrastructure. Progress is being made in extending affordable water access to underserved regions, but much remains to be done. Overcoming the remaining barriers to water security could alleviate disease worldwide and contribute to economic development.",
    "explanation": "✅ Doğru cevap: D) maintains\n\n🔎 Neden doğru? 'perpetuates a vicious cycle' ifadesi, kısır döngünün sürmesini/devam etmesini sağlamak anlamına gelir; bu nedenle 'maintains' (sürdürür) en yakın anlamlı seçenektir.\n\n❌ Diğer seçenekler neden yanlış?\n\nA) excludes: dışlar\n\nB) terminates: sonlandırır\n\nC) plummets: aniden düşer\n\nE) contradicts: çelişir\n\n🧠 YDS taktiği: Bağlamdan kelime anlamı sorularında, altı çizili kelimenin cümledeki işlevi (olumlu/olumsuz, devam ettirici/sonlandırıcı) belirlenmelidir.\n\n📌 Öğrenilmesi gereken kelime/kalıp: perpetuate (v.): sürdürmek, devam ettirmek\n\nOkuma Parçası Sorusu (Ayrıntı)\n\nDuring the 20th century, numerous engineering breakthroughs in water treatment made it possible to purify or at least significantly improve most of the water sources that have sickened or killed millions of people each year. But the ability to access those treatment systems is concentrated in relatively affluent regions, where the vast majority of water infrastructure investment occurs. The term water security, therefore, encompasses the array of problems faced by the world's most water-stressed inhabitants, who often cannot obtain or do not have access to clean water that could greatly reduce the disease burden under which they suffer. The problems include deficient distribution infrastructure, imbalances between population growth and supply, and the lack of incentive to build treatment facilities in regions with limited economic return. By expanding access to available water interventions, and especially basic sanitation, health officials could prevent millions of deaths annually. Lack of access to clean water and complementary sanitation in turn perpetuates a vicious cycle: poor health impairs productivity and economic development, while low productivity keeps the citizens of the least-developed regions too poor to afford appropriate infrastructure. Progress is being made in extending affordable water access to underserved regions, but much remains to be done. Overcoming the remaining barriers to water security could alleviate disease worldwide and contribute to economic development.",
