    "questionText": "Boşluk için en uygun seçeneği işaretleyiniz.\n\nThe clownfish is a small, brightly coloured fish that lives among the stinging tentacles of sea anemones on coral reefs. What makes this relationship unusual is that the clownfish is immune to the anemone's sting due to a protective mucus coating on its skin. In exchange for shelter, the clownfish chases away small fish that might otherwise nibble on the anemone's tentacles. ---- By providing this protection, the clownfish helps ensure that its host anemone continues to thrive, which in turn secures the clownfish's own safe habitat.",
