    "questionText": "Disiplinler arası bir çalışma ortamı sizi başlangıçta farklı yöntemleri dikkate almaya zorlar ve en sonunda bulgularınızı çok daha anlaşılır şekilde sunmanıza yardımcı olur.",
    "options": {
      "A": "An interdisciplinary work environment is what forces the consideration of different methods to begin with and helps you to present your findings more clearly in the end.",
      "B": "An interdisciplinary work environment forces you to consider different methods to begin with and helps you to present your findings more clearly in the end.",
      "C": "An interdisciplinary work environment not only forces you to consider different methods, but also helps you to present your findings quite clearly in the end.",
      "D": "In the beginning, you are forced to consider different methods in an interdisciplinary work environment and this helps you to present your findings quite clearly in the end.",
      "E": "Being forced to consider different methods as you begin with an interdisciplinary work environment helps you to present your findings in a pretty clearer way in the end."
    },
    "correctAnswer": "B",
    "solutionMethod": "✅ Doğru cevap: B) An interdisciplinary work environment forces you to consider different methods to begin with and helps you to present your findings more clearly in the end.\n\n🔎 Neden doğru? Doğru çeviri, Türkçe cümledeki 'sizi...zorlar ve...yardımcı olur' yapısını, öznenin 'ortam' olduğu basit bir İngilizce cümleyle ('forces you to... and helps you to...') aktarır.\n\n❌ Diğer seçenekler neden yanlış?\n\nA) 'is what forces' vurgu yapısı gereksiz yere eklenmiş, orijinal cümlenin daha doğrudan yapısını bozmaktadır.\n\nC) 'not only... but also' yapısı orijinalde olmayan bir vurgu ekler.\n\nD) Cümle sırası değiştirilmiş, 'başlangıçta' zarfının konumu anlamı hafifçe bozmaktadır.\n\nE) 'Being forced to' ile başlayan yapı, orijinal cümledeki nesnenin ('ortam') özne olma rolünü değiştirir.\n\n🧠 YDS taktiği: Türkçedeki bağlı iki yüklemli cümleler ('zorlar ve yardımcı olur'), İngilizceye genellikle 'and' ile bağlanan iki fiil yapısıyla aktarılır.\n\n📌 Öğrenilmesi gereken kelime/kalıp: interdisciplinary (adj.): disiplinler arası\n\n43-46: Okuma Parçası Sorusu\n\nOkuma Parçası Sorusu (Ayrıntı)\n\nUrban green spaces are not neutral in their impact on city life. The educational, physical, and mental health effects on individuals who spend time in parks and community gardens can have positive effects on the wellbeing of a whole neighbourhood. Likewise, green spaces can be mismanaged. Wildlife can be adversely affected, as in some instances of disturbance by loud events or off-leash pets, and of overuse of fragile lawns. Paths and picnic areas can be expanded, resulting in the loss of native vegetation and soil compaction. Trees can be damaged by careless maintenance. Irrigation systems can fail, leading to problems of water waste and soil erosion. Visitors can introduce litter and other pollutants into ponds and streams within parks. The sheer number of people using urban parks means that heavy foot traffic covers much of the green space, and without careful and considered use, significant impacts to the ecosystem can occur. A major challenge for city planners is to help residents enjoy their green spaces, but in ways that minimise negative impacts on local ecosystems. Many measures, from educational signage to the design of pathways, can be effective in this work. The community-based stewardship model helps focus on the benefits that are to be realised and the appropriate supportive management techniques.",
    "explanation": "✅ Doğru cevap: B) An interdisciplinary work environment forces you to consider different methods to begin with and helps you to present your findings more clearly in the end.\n\n🔎 Neden doğru? Doğru çeviri, Türkçe cümledeki 'sizi...zorlar ve...yardımcı olur' yapısını, öznenin 'ortam' olduğu basit bir İngilizce cümleyle ('forces you to... and helps you to...') aktarır.\n\n❌ Diğer seçenekler neden yanlış?\n\nA) 'is what forces' vurgu yapısı gereksiz yere eklenmiş, orijinal cümlenin daha doğrudan yapısını bozmaktadır.\n\nC) 'not only... but also' yapısı orijinalde olmayan bir vurgu ekler.\n\nD) Cümle sırası değiştirilmiş, 'başlangıçta' zarfının konumu anlamı hafifçe bozmaktadır.\n\nE) 'Being forced to' ile başlayan yapı, orijinal cümledeki nesnenin ('ortam') özne olma rolünü değiştirir.\n\n🧠 YDS taktiği: Türkçedeki bağlı iki yüklemli cümleler ('zorlar ve yardımcı olur'), İngilizceye genellikle 'and' ile bağlanan iki fiil yapısıyla aktarılır.\n\n📌 Öğrenilmesi gereken kelime/kalıp: interdisciplinary (adj.): disiplinler arası\n\n43-46: Okuma Parçası Sorusu\n\nOkuma Parçası Sorusu (Ayrıntı)\n\nUrban green spaces are not neutral in their impact on city life. The educational, physical, and mental health effects on individuals who spend time in parks and community gardens can have positive effects on the wellbeing of a whole neighbourhood. Likewise, green spaces can be mismanaged. Wildlife can be adversely affected, as in some instances of disturbance by loud events or off-leash pets, and of overuse of fragile lawns. Paths and picnic areas can be expanded, resulting in the loss of native vegetation and soil compaction. Trees can be damaged by careless maintenance. Irrigation systems can fail, leading to problems of water waste and soil erosion. Visitors can introduce litter and other pollutants into ponds and streams within parks. The sheer number of people using urban parks means that heavy foot traffic covers much of the green space, and without careful and considered use, significant impacts to the ecosystem can occur. A major challenge for city planners is to help residents enjoy their green spaces, but in ways that minimise negative impacts on local ecosystems. Many measures, from educational signage to the design of pathways, can be effective in this work. The community-based stewardship model helps focus on the benefits that are to be realised and the appropriate supportive management techniques.",
