    "questionText": "Naomi:\n I wonder what would happen if bees disappeared completely.\n\nTheo:\n Well, I was reading an article about it and it said plant species that rely heavily on pollinators would be hit hardest.\n\nNaomi:\n How is that?\n\nTheo:\n ----\n\nNaomi:\n I see. So this probably means they'll be outcompeted by wind-pollinated plants, and the animals that feed on them will likely decline too.",
    "options": {
      "A": "To be honest, I'm not sure, but one theory holds that pollination evolved because it helped early flowering plants survive environmental shocks.",
      "B": "You know many flowering plants rely on pollinators to reproduce. Without bees, those plants won't be pollinated, and they might be replaced by wind-pollinated species that don't need insects.",
      "C": "The animals that were closer to bees helped individuals and themselves to reproduce in large colonies. This was proof enough that they had good genes.",
      "D": "The decades following a pollinator collapse would be marked by crop failures, price spikes and food shortages of varying severity. I mean all the consequences that beekeeping has left behind.",
      "E": "I can say traces of bees will remain, even decades after their disappearance. For instance, microbes will need lots of time to consume all the wax and honey they've left behind."
    },
    "correctAnswer": "B",
    "solutionMethod": "✅ Doğru cevap: B) You know many flowering plants rely on pollinators to reproduce. Without bees, those plants won't be pollinated, and they might be replaced by wind-pollinated species that don't need insects.\n\n🔎 Neden doğru? Theo'nun yanıtı, tozlaşma olmadan bu bitkilerin üreyemeyeceğini ve rüzgarla tozlaşan türlerle yer değiştirebileceğini açıklamalıdır; bu da Naomi'nin sonraki 'outcompeted by wind-pollinated plants' çıkarımına zemin hazırlayan (B)'dir.\n\n❌ Diğer seçenekler neden yanlış?\n\nA) belirsiz bir teori sunar, Naomi'nin sonraki 'rüzgarla tozlaşan bitkiler' çıkarımına zemin hazırlamaz\n\nC) hayvanların üremesiyle ilgili ayrı bir konu, bitkilerin rekabetiyle bağlantılı değil\n\nD) sonuçları sayar ama bitkilerin neden rekabette geride kalacağını açıklamaz\n\nE) bal ve balmumu kalıntılarından söz eder, bitki rekabetiyle ilgili değildir\n\n🧠 YDS taktiği: Boşluktan sonraki repliğin 'so this probably means...' ile bir çıkarım yapması durumunda, boşluğun bu çıkarımın dayanağı olan somut bilgiyi içermesi gerekir.\n\n📌 Öğrenilmesi gereken kelime/kalıp: be outcompeted by X: X tarafından rekabette geride bırakılmak\n\nDiyalog Tamamlama Sorusu",
