    "questionText": "Adaptive Learning Systems (ALS) are the discipline of combining assessment, personalisation, and feedback into a system capable of answering these two fundamental questions: “What does this learner already know?” and “What is the best next lesson for them?” To build such a system, we first need to understand the methods and techniques that enable assessment, personalisation, and feedback. At first glance, this subject matter is nothing new, as hundreds of books and articles have been written on educational assessment, personalised learning, feedback techniques, and so forth. ---- ALS addresses this very issue.",
