    "questionText": "(I) Students of all ages sometimes fear the challenge of high-stakes, timed examinations. (II) Teachers can help reduce unrealistic fears by pointing out how common they are among students and what strategies help reduce such fears by providing opportunities for students to practise under timed conditions individually or in small groups. (III) Thus, students can practise managing their time while answering questions and reviewing their work. (IV) Students need to know how different examination formats vary from one another and how particular subjects call for different revision strategies. (V) Practising under timed conditions in these ways can lessen students' anxieties while, at the same time, helping them to learn the subject matter of the lesson.",
