    "questionText": "With few exceptions, the Austronesian languages are closely related to one another. Despite their very large number and the vast expanse of territory they occupy, it is fairly easy to recognise their shared genetic origin. ---- As a result, the total number of Austronesian languages remains a contentious issue. Taking this into account, the approximate number of Austronesian languages in a given area, and the number of their speakers there, could only be determined through a wide-scale scientific study.",
