    "questionText": "(I) In the late 15th century, when Europeans first arrived in the Western Hemisphere, Mesoamerica was dominated by the vast Aztec empire. (II) Today, many people in both Mesoamerica and along the Caribbean are of mixed heritage. (III) But within decades of the Europeans' arrival, Spanish conquerors had overwhelmed the Aztecs and every other major group. (IV) Native Aztec, Zapotec, Mixtec, and other peoples were gathered into European-style villages and towns and forcibly converted to Roman Catholicism. (V) Europeans also introduced new sources of income, however, making these peoples no longer dependent solely on traditional agriculture.",
