    "questionText": "(I) Nobody knows exactly where music came from because there are no written records. (II) A good guess would be that thousands of years ago, primitive peoples used music in much the same way as we use it now: to communicate, to pass time while working, to express joy or sadness, or to mark a special occasion. (III) Flutes were among the earliest instruments found in all parts of the world. (IV) The first instrument was the one every person is born with — the body. (V) We have voices to sing and shout with, hands to clap, and feet to stamp, and this is enough to create melody and rhythm, the two basic elements of music.",
