    "questionText": "(I) The ancient Olympic Games, known to us through ancient literature, art, and modern archaeology, were the oldest and most prestigious athletic competition of the ancient world. (II) Although they inspired the modern Olympics, the ancient games need to be understood within their own ancient Greek cultural context. (III) Contrary to popular belief, the ancient Olympics differed considerably from their modern counterpart in structure, events, and underlying purpose. (IV) The permanent site of the ancient Olympics was an isolated religious sanctuary along the Alpheios River, in the territory of the state of Elis in southwestern Greece. (V) With sacred rites and crowns of olive leaves as prizes, the ancient Olympic Games formed part of a major religious festival honouring Zeus, the chief god of the Greeks.",
