    "questionText": "(I) Around the world, people welcomed the end of the Cold War with a deep sense of relief. (II) By almost any measure, the conflict had shaped global politics for nearly half a century. (III) The most commonly accepted starting point for the Cold War is 1947, marking the beginning of open ideological rivalry between the two superpowers. (IV) The economic cost of maintaining rival military alliances has been estimated in the trillions of dollars. (V) In human terms, proxy conflicts linked to the rivalry claimed millions of lives across multiple continents.",
