    "questionText": "(I) The best conditions for milkweed seeds are relatively calm, warm afternoons that generate gentle updraughts. (II) A 2010 study at a Midwestern university found that most milkweed seeds land within 15 metres of their parent plant. (III) That is because the seed's silky floss slows its fall to about 25 cm per second, and milkweed plants grow around a metre tall. (IV) So, that gives each seed several seconds of flight time to be carried sideways by the wind toward a new location. (V) Higher wind speeds do not necessarily increase how far the seeds travel, because strong gusts tend to push seeds downward as well as sideways, causing them to land sooner.",
