    "questionText": "(I) Established on 11 December 1946, the United Nations Children's Fund (UNICEF) is one of the original agencies of the United Nations. (II) UNICEF defines its mission not merely as emergency relief, but as long-term support for children's health, education, and protection. (III) Headquartered in New York City, United States, UNICEF was set up to provide relief to children affected by the aftermath of the Second World War. (IV) It later expanded its mandate to address the long-term needs of children in developing countries around the world. (V) Earlier relief agencies had focused mainly on food distribution, medical supplies, and clothing for war-affected populations.",
    "options": {
      "A": "I",
      "B": "II",
      "C": "III",
      "D": "IV",
      "E": "V"
    },
